# Build-time public configuration.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at build time, so
# nothing secret can live here. This file is committed on purpose: a GA4
# Measurement ID is a public identifier that appears in the HTML of every page
# the property tracks, so keeping it in the repo leaks nothing and means a fresh
# clone or a new Vercel project reports to the right property with no dashboard
# setup.
#
# Anything set in the Vercel dashboard takes precedence over this file, because
# Next.js will not overwrite a variable that is already present in the process
# environment. So this is a default, not a lock-in.
#
# Real secrets (if any are ever needed) belong in .env.local, which is already
# gitignored via the "*.local" rule, or in Vercel's encrypted env vars.

# Google Analytics 4 — property created 2026-07.
# Conversions and UTM attribution run through this; see lib/analytics.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-96QK8PY0XH
